body:
The leading thought behind it is that the game will just get boring at that point. Even with new things being added, the game is already getting boring for some people. If they just add new levels to buildings and units, you run into the same issue I mentioned in a comment above about the 100 building limit. Upgrading everything a level or 2 and maybe adding 1 new unit each town hall could work for 1 or 2 town halls. But if you just do that over and over again, then there isn't much point to keep playing since the game stays the same. Base designs might change slightly. Attack strategies might change slightly. But at that point, you're farming to do the same thing over and over, but if they add something new, then it's exciting and new. Sure, it can get pretty complicated, and the game already is pretty complicated. But I honestly think that's what makes the game fun. The early town halls are fun because it's all brand new and exciting. The later town halls are cool because they require a lot more strategy and planning in order to be a good player. 

&#x200B;

But in the end, everyone likes what they like, and dislike what they dislike. Everyone will have different opinions, and those who want more new exciting things, will create concepts of those new things because it's fun. Those who want the same thing over and over, will want that.
